# MapStruct for entity ↔ DTO

In `service/organization-panel-service`, **use MapStruct** for converting between JPA entities and DTOs. Do not hand-write field-by-field mapping methods in services or controllers.

## Required patterns

- Put mappers under `.../mapper/` (e.g. `UserMapper`).
- Define interfaces with `@Mapper(componentModel = "spring")` and inject them via constructor (`@RequiredArgsConstructor`).
- Prefer `toDto` / `toEntity` (or `toResponse` / `toRequest`) naming consistent with existing mappers.
- Keep MapStruct on the classpath (`org.mapstruct:mapstruct`) and configure the annotation processor alongside Lombok in `pom.xml` (`lombok-mapstruct-binding` when both are used).
- Use `@Mapping` only when names differ or a field needs a custom expression; avoid unnecessary annotations.
- For lists/pages, map via the mapper (`mapper.toDto(entity)`, `page.map(mapper::toDto)`), not manual loops that copy fields.

## Examples

```java
// ❌ BAD — hand-written mapping in the service
private UserResponse toResponse(User user) {
  return new UserResponse(
      user.getId(),
      user.getFirstName(),
      user.getLastName(),
      user.getMobile(),
      user.getNationalId(),
      user.getBirthDate(),
      user.getStatus());
}
```

```java
// ✅ GOOD — MapStruct mapper
@Mapper(componentModel = "spring")
public interface UserMapper {
  UserResponse toResponse(User user);
}

@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class UserService {
  private final UserMapper userMapper;

  // ...
  return PageResponse.map(result, pageNumber, userMapper::toResponse);
}
```
